---
import SiteLayout from '../layouts/SiteLayout.astro';
import legacyPages from '../data/legacy-pages.json';
import pageStyle from '../styles/pages/privacy.css?url';
const page = legacyPages['privacy.html'];
---

<SiteLayout {...page} pageStyle={pageStyle} legacy={true} noindex={false}>
  <main id="main" class="content">
    <p class="overline">Legal</p>
    <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
    <section>
      <h2>HR services within your infrastructure</h2><p>
        For People Setup, Hiring Support and Founder Voice engagements, we work
        within the client’s infrastructure and agreed access. Please do not send
        employee records, payroll data, appraisal files or confidential company
        documents through this website.
      </p><p>
        Initial service enquiries collect contact details, the selected service
        and a non-confidential brief. Recruitment remains a separate workflow
        with explicit CV and JD submission forms and the private storage
        described below.
      </p>
    </section>

    <p class="meta">Last updated: 25 October 2026 · Quantum Leaps, Mumbai</p>

    <div class="highlight">
      <p>
        Plain English summary: We only collect information you choose to give
        us. We use it to contact you about your enquiry. We never sell your
        data. You can ask us to delete it at any time.
      </p>
    </div>

    <h2>1. Who we are</h2>
    <p>
      <strong>Quantum Leaps</strong> is a specialist recruitment agency based in
      Mumbai, India. We hire for marketing, creative, design and technology teams
      across India.
    </p>
    <p>
      Quantum Leaps is responsible for handling the recruitment information you
      submit through this website.
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>Email: <a href="mailto:contact@qleaps.in">contact@qleaps.in</a></li>
      <li>Phone: <a href="tel:+919930822894">+91 99308 22894</a></li>
      <li>Address: Mumbai, India</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>2. What data we collect</h2>
    <p>
      We collect the following personal data when you submit a hiring enquiry or
      candidate application on our website:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Name</strong> — to address you correctly</li>
      <li><strong>Email address</strong> — to respond to your enquiry</li>
      <li><strong>Message content</strong> — to understand your request</li>
      <li>
        <strong>Company, hiring brief and job details</strong> — to review an employer
        enquiry or job posting. Approved company names and job details are displayed
        publicly; employer contact details are kept separate.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Candidate details</strong> — phone, city, specialism, experience,
        desired role, current title, LinkedIn or portfolio links, notice period,
        relocation preferences, target compensation and the CV you attach
      </li>
      <li><strong>Consent record</strong> — that you agreed to be contacted</li>
      <li>
        <strong>Submission timestamp and random receipt token</strong> — for security
        and fraud prevention
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      Our forms submit information to our Google Apps Script handler. Candidate
      CVs are stored in Google Drive and application records are linked to the
      role applied for. Where supported, a random submission token is used to
      retrieve a non-personal status and reference. If receipt cannot be
      confirmed, the website says so.
    </p>

    <h2>3. Why we collect it</h2>
    <p>We process your personal data for the following purposes:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>To respond to your enquiry</strong> — to handle your request
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>To discuss relevant recruitment opportunities</strong> — with your
        consent for recruitment contact
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>To prevent fraud and spam</strong> — to protect the service
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2>4. How we use your data</h2>
    <p>We will use your name and email to:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Respond to your message, typically within 2 business days</li>
      <li>
        Contact you about relevant roles or hiring opportunities (if you
        consented)
      </li>
      <li>Review candidate applications and discuss relevant opportunities</li>
    </ul>
    <p>We will <strong>never</strong>:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Sell your data to third parties</li>
      <li>
        Share it with other recruiters or job platforms without your consent
      </li>
      <li>Use it for any purpose unrelated to your original enquiry</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>5. Who we share data with</h2>
    <p>
      We use the following services to operate this website and process
      submissions:
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>Google Apps Script and Google workspace services</strong> — process
        form submissions and attached CVs through our configured Google integration
        (<a
          href="https://policies.google.com/privacy"
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener">privacy policy</a
        >)
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Netlify</strong> — website hosting (<a
          href="https://www.netlify.com/privacy/"
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener">privacy policy</a
        >)
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2>6. How long we keep your data</h2>
    <p>
      We review enquiry and application records periodically and aim to retain
      them only while relevant to recruitment or necessary record keeping.
      Retention and deletion are managed by our team, not an automatic expiry
      feature of this website. If you ask us to delete your data, we will do so
      within 30 days.
    </p>

    <h2>7. Your rights</h2>
    <p>You have the right to:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>Access</strong> — request a copy of the personal data we hold about
        you
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Rectification</strong> — ask us to correct inaccurate data
      </li>
      <li><strong>Erasure</strong> — ask us to delete your data</li>
      <li>
        <strong>Withdraw consent</strong> — opt out of marketing at any time
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Object</strong> — to processing based on legitimate interest
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Portability</strong> — receive your data in a structured format
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      To exercise any right, email us at <a href="mailto:contact@qleaps.in"
        >contact@qleaps.in</a
      >. We will respond within 30 days.
    </p>

    <h2>8. Contact preferences</h2>
    <p>You can ask us to stop recruitment communications at any time by:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>
        Emailing us at <a href="mailto:contact@qleaps.in">contact@qleaps.in</a> with
        the subject "Unsubscribe"
      </li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      Withdrawal of consent does not affect the lawfulness of processing before
      withdrawal.
    </p>

    <h2>9. Cookies</h2>
    <p>
      This website does not set analytics or advertising cookies. Submitted
      information is processed through the Google integration described above.
    </p>

    <h2>10. Security</h2>
    <p>
      The production site uses HTTPS. Forms are sent to our Google Apps Script
      handler, which validates submitted fields and file size/format before
      storing records in Google Sheets and files in private Google Drive
      folders. File validation is not a malware scan. Access is limited to
      authorised team members; we do not publish CV links in the public jobs
      feed.
    </p>

    <h2>11. Changes to this policy</h2>
    <p>
      We may update this policy from time to time. The "Last updated" date at
      the top will always reflect when changes were made. Significant changes
      will be communicated by email if we have your contact details.
    </p>

    <h2>12. Contact</h2>
    <p>
      Questions about this policy? Email <a href="mailto:contact@qleaps.in"
        >contact@qleaps.in</a
      > or call <a href="tel:+919930822894">+91 99308 22894</a>.
    </p>
  </main>
</SiteLayout>
